{"slug": "cap-theorem", "voice": "bf_emma", "accent": "uk", "sampleRate": 24000, "duration": 273.875, "contentHash": "dc8c89db82ece9b5808365ade40a5d969d90d7ae201f24242897536089dd931f", "blocks": [{"index": 0, "kind": "title", "text": "The CAP Theorem", "start": 0.0, "end": 2.1, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 0.225, "end": 0.362}, {"text": "CAP", "start": 0.362, "end": 1.0}, {"text": "Theorem", "start": 1.0, "end": 1.85}]}, {"index": 1, "kind": "summary", "text": "Why a distributed data store can only pick two of consistency, availability, and partition tolerance — and what that trade-off means in practice.", "start": 2.1, "end": 11.125, "words": [{"text": "Why", "start": 2.35, "end": 2.538}, {"text": "a", "start": 2.538, "end": 2.6}, {"text": "distributed", "start": 2.6, "end": 3.2}, {"text": "data", "start": 3.2, "end": 3.55}, {"text": "store", "start": 3.55, "end": 3.925}, {"text": "can", "start": 3.925, "end": 4.05}, {"text": "only", "start": 4.05, "end": 4.35}, {"text": "pick", "start": 4.35, "end": 4.588}, {"text": "two", "start": 4.588, "end": 4.812}, {"text": "of", "start": 4.812, "end": 4.9}, {"text": "consistency", "start": 4.9, "end": 5.825}, {"text": "availability", "start": 5.825, "end": 6.725}, {"text": "and", "start": 6.725, "end": 6.875}, {"text": "partition", "start": 6.875, "end": 7.375}, {"text": "tolerance", "start": 7.375, "end": 8.387}, {"text": "and", "start": 8.387, "end": 8.6}, {"text": "what", "start": 8.6, "end": 8.75}, {"text": "that", "start": 8.75, "end": 8.95}, {"text": "trade", "start": 8.95, "end": 9.4}, {"text": "off", "start": 9.4, "end": 9.4}, {"text": "means", "start": 9.4, "end": 9.662}, {"text": "in", "start": 9.662, "end": 9.775}, {"text": "practice", "start": 9.775, "end": 10.825}]}, {"index": 2, "kind": "prose", "text": "Why this matters", "start": 11.125, "end": 13.05, "words": [{"text": "Why", "start": 11.375, "end": 11.6}, {"text": "this", "start": 11.6, "end": 11.8}, {"text": "matters", "start": 11.8, "end": 12.8}]}, {"index": 3, "kind": "prose", "text": "Sooner or later you'll read an outage postmortem or a database marketing page that says something like \"we chose availability over consistency during the incident.\" The CAP theorem is what gives that sentence meaning. It's the single most quoted idea in distributed systems — you'll hear it in interviews, design reviews, and conference talks. Half the people who mention it get it slightly wrong. (Not you. Not after this lesson.)", "start": 13.05, "end": 36.875, "words": [{"text": "Sooner", "start": 13.35, "end": 13.65}, {"text": "or", "start": 13.65, "end": 13.775}, {"text": "later", "start": 13.775, "end": 14.125}, {"text": "you'll", "start": 14.125, "end": 14.275}, {"text": "read", "start": 14.275, "end": 14.488}, {"text": "an", "start": 14.488, "end": 14.575}, {"text": "outage", "start": 14.575, "end": 14.975}, {"text": "postmortem", "start": 14.975, "end": 15.675}, {"text": "or", "start": 15.675, "end": 15.788}, {"text": "a", "start": 15.788, "end": 15.85}, {"text": "database", "start": 15.85, "end": 16.375}, {"text": "marketing", "start": 16.375, "end": 16.8}, {"text": "page", "start": 16.8, "end": 17.15}, {"text": "that", "start": 17.15, "end": 17.275}, {"text": "says", "start": 17.275, "end": 17.475}, {"text": "something", "start": 17.475, "end": 17.8}, {"text": "like", "start": 17.8, "end": 18.275}, {"text": "we", "start": 18.275, "end": 18.425}, {"text": "chose", "start": 18.425, "end": 18.688}, {"text": "availability", "start": 18.688, "end": 19.363}, {"text": "over", "start": 19.363, "end": 19.575}, {"text": "consistency", "start": 19.575, "end": 20.25}, {"text": "during", "start": 20.25, "end": 20.488}, {"text": "the", "start": 20.488, "end": 20.575}, {"text": "incident", "start": 20.575, "end": 21.625}, {"text": "The", "start": 21.625, "end": 21.888}, {"text": "CAP", "start": 21.888, "end": 22.475}, {"text": "theorem", "start": 22.475, "end": 22.85}, {"text": "is", "start": 22.85, "end": 22.962}, {"text": "what", "start": 22.962, "end": 23.1}, {"text": "gives", "start": 23.1, "end": 23.325}, {"text": "that", "start": 23.325, "end": 23.55}, {"text": "sentence", "start": 23.55, "end": 23.975}, {"text": "meaning", "start": 23.975, "end": 24.675}, {"text": "It's", "start": 24.675, "end": 24.888}, {"text": "the", "start": 24.888, "end": 24.975}, {"text": "single", "start": 24.975, "end": 25.325}, {"text": "most", "start": 25.325, "end": 25.55}, {"text": "quoted", "start": 25.55, "end": 25.913}, {"text": "idea", "start": 25.913, "end": 26.3}, {"text": "in", "start": 26.3, "end": 26.388}, {"text": "distributed", "start": 26.388, "end": 27.0}, {"text": "systems", "start": 27.0, "end": 27.775}, {"text": "you'll", "start": 27.775, "end": 28.0}, {"text": "hear", "start": 28.0, "end": 28.225}, {"text": "it", "start": 28.225, "end": 28.35}, {"text": "in", "start": 28.35, "end": 28.45}, {"text": "interviews", "start": 28.45, "end": 28.925}, {"text": "design", "start": 28.925, "end": 29.312}, {"text": "reviews", "start": 29.312, "end": 29.7}, {"text": "and", "start": 29.7, "end": 29.85}, {"text": "conference", "start": 29.85, "end": 30.325}, {"text": "talks", "start": 30.325, "end": 31.2}, {"text": "Half", "start": 31.2, "end": 31.538}, {"text": "the", "start": 31.538, "end": 31.625}, {"text": "people", "start": 31.625, "end": 31.938}, {"text": "who", "start": 31.938, "end": 32.075}, {"text": "mention", "start": 32.075, "end": 32.425}, {"text": "it", "start": 32.425, "end": 32.55}, {"text": "get", "start": 32.55, "end": 32.713}, {"text": "it", "start": 32.713, "end": 32.825}, {"text": "slightly", "start": 32.825, "end": 33.2}, {"text": "wrong", "start": 33.2, "end": 33.975}, {"text": "Not", "start": 33.975, "end": 34.362}, {"text": "you", "start": 34.362, "end": 34.9}, {"text": "Not", "start": 34.9, "end": 35.225}, {"text": "after", "start": 35.225, "end": 35.487}, {"text": "this", "start": 35.487, "end": 35.675}, {"text": "lesson", "start": 35.675, "end": 36.55}]}, {"index": 4, "kind": "prose", "text": "Picture a restaurant chain", "start": 36.875, "end": 39.3, "words": [{"text": "Picture", "start": 37.1, "end": 37.5}, {"text": "a", "start": 37.5, "end": 37.6}, {"text": "restaurant", "start": 37.6, "end": 38.188}, {"text": "chain", "start": 38.188, "end": 39.025}]}, {"index": 5, "kind": "prose", "text": "This lesson's running analogy: you run a tiny restaurant chain with two diners across town, sharing one menu. Let's define the CAP properties in diner terms:", "start": 39.3, "end": 49.75, "words": [{"text": "This", "start": 39.55, "end": 39.725}, {"text": "lesson's", "start": 39.725, "end": 40.15}, {"text": "running", "start": 40.15, "end": 40.45}, {"text": "analogy", "start": 40.45, "end": 41.3}, {"text": "you", "start": 41.3, "end": 41.525}, {"text": "run", "start": 41.525, "end": 41.712}, {"text": "a", "start": 41.712, "end": 41.775}, {"text": "tiny", "start": 41.775, "end": 42.1}, {"text": "restaurant", "start": 42.1, "end": 42.537}, {"text": "chain", "start": 42.537, "end": 42.862}, {"text": "with", "start": 42.862, "end": 43.0}, {"text": "two", "start": 43.0, "end": 43.2}, {"text": "diners", "start": 43.2, "end": 43.537}, {"text": "across", "start": 43.537, "end": 43.875}, {"text": "town", "start": 43.875, "end": 44.375}, {"text": "sharing", "start": 44.375, "end": 44.9}, {"text": "one", "start": 44.9, "end": 45.1}, {"text": "menu", "start": 45.1, "end": 46.0}, {"text": "Let's", "start": 46.0, "end": 46.4}, {"text": "define", "start": 46.4, "end": 46.762}, {"text": "the", "start": 46.762, "end": 46.862}, {"text": "CAP", "start": 46.862, "end": 47.45}, {"text": "properties", "start": 47.45, "end": 48.025}, {"text": "in", "start": 48.025, "end": 48.175}, {"text": "diner", "start": 48.175, "end": 48.5}, {"text": "terms", "start": 48.5, "end": 49.45}]}, {"index": 6, "kind": "prose", "text": "Consistency (C) — Both diners' menu boards always show the same specials. If the lunch special changes, every customer at every diner sees the update at the same time. Nobody orders a dish that was cancelled ten minutes ago.", "start": 49.75, "end": 63.675, "words": [{"text": "Consistency", "start": 50.0, "end": 50.775}, {"text": "C", "start": 50.775, "end": 51.275}, {"text": "Both", "start": 51.275, "end": 51.7}, {"text": "diners", "start": 51.7, "end": 52.05}, {"text": "menu", "start": 52.05, "end": 52.35}, {"text": "boards", "start": 52.35, "end": 52.675}, {"text": "always", "start": 52.675, "end": 53.038}, {"text": "show", "start": 53.038, "end": 53.263}, {"text": "the", "start": 53.263, "end": 53.35}, {"text": "same", "start": 53.35, "end": 53.625}, {"text": "specials", "start": 53.625, "end": 54.625}, {"text": "If", "start": 54.625, "end": 54.9}, {"text": "the", "start": 54.9, "end": 55.0}, {"text": "lunch", "start": 55.0, "end": 55.3}, {"text": "special", "start": 55.3, "end": 55.688}, {"text": "changes", "start": 55.688, "end": 56.45}, {"text": "every", "start": 56.45, "end": 56.875}, {"text": "customer", "start": 56.875, "end": 57.35}, {"text": "at", "start": 57.35, "end": 57.475}, {"text": "every", "start": 57.475, "end": 57.75}, {"text": "diner", "start": 57.75, "end": 58.112}, {"text": "sees", "start": 58.112, "end": 58.388}, {"text": "the", "start": 58.388, "end": 58.5}, {"text": "update", "start": 58.5, "end": 58.938}, {"text": "at", "start": 58.938, "end": 59.013}, {"text": "the", "start": 59.013, "end": 59.1}, {"text": "same", "start": 59.1, "end": 59.4}, {"text": "time", "start": 59.4, "end": 60.25}, {"text": "Nobody", "start": 60.25, "end": 60.725}, {"text": "orders", "start": 60.725, "end": 61.013}, {"text": "a", "start": 61.013, "end": 61.075}, {"text": "dish", "start": 61.075, "end": 61.35}, {"text": "that", "start": 61.35, "end": 61.462}, {"text": "was", "start": 61.462, "end": 61.6}, {"text": "cancelled", "start": 61.6, "end": 62.087}, {"text": "ten", "start": 62.087, "end": 62.312}, {"text": "minutes", "start": 62.312, "end": 62.587}, {"text": "ago", "start": 62.587, "end": 63.375}]}, {"index": 7, "kind": "prose", "text": "Availability (A) — Every diner always seats every customer and takes every order, no exceptions. Nobody is turned away or told to \"come back later.\"", "start": 63.675, "end": 73.35, "words": [{"text": "Availability", "start": 63.95, "end": 64.675}, {"text": "A", "start": 64.675, "end": 65.225}, {"text": "Every", "start": 65.225, "end": 65.725}, {"text": "diner", "start": 65.725, "end": 66.05}, {"text": "always", "start": 66.05, "end": 66.375}, {"text": "seats", "start": 66.375, "end": 66.675}, {"text": "every", "start": 66.675, "end": 66.95}, {"text": "customer", "start": 66.95, "end": 67.45}, {"text": "and", "start": 67.45, "end": 67.575}, {"text": "takes", "start": 67.575, "end": 67.9}, {"text": "every", "start": 67.9, "end": 68.2}, {"text": "order", "start": 68.2, "end": 68.525}, {"text": "no", "start": 68.525, "end": 68.775}, {"text": "exceptions", "start": 68.775, "end": 69.9}, {"text": "Nobody", "start": 69.9, "end": 70.375}, {"text": "is", "start": 70.375, "end": 70.525}, {"text": "turned", "start": 70.525, "end": 70.763}, {"text": "away", "start": 70.763, "end": 71.075}, {"text": "or", "start": 71.075, "end": 71.2}, {"text": "told", "start": 71.2, "end": 71.55}, {"text": "to", "start": 71.55, "end": 71.662}, {"text": "come", "start": 71.662, "end": 71.875}, {"text": "back", "start": 71.875, "end": 72.1}, {"text": "later", "start": 72.1, "end": 72.95}]}, {"index": 8, "kind": "prose", "text": "Partition tolerance (P) — The system keeps working even if the phone line between the two diners is cut and they can't talk to each other.", "start": 73.35, "end": 81.55, "words": [{"text": "Partition", "start": 73.6, "end": 74.075}, {"text": "tolerance", "start": 74.075, "end": 74.65}, {"text": "P", "start": 74.65, "end": 75.375}, {"text": "The", "start": 75.375, "end": 75.6}, {"text": "system", "start": 75.6, "end": 75.95}, {"text": "keeps", "start": 75.95, "end": 76.225}, {"text": "working", "start": 76.225, "end": 76.625}, {"text": "even", "start": 76.625, "end": 76.912}, {"text": "if", "start": 76.912, "end": 77.012}, {"text": "the", "start": 77.012, "end": 77.137}, {"text": "phone", "start": 77.137, "end": 77.45}, {"text": "line", "start": 77.45, "end": 77.662}, {"text": "between", "start": 77.662, "end": 77.938}, {"text": "the", "start": 77.938, "end": 78.025}, {"text": "two", "start": 78.025, "end": 78.225}, {"text": "diners", "start": 78.225, "end": 78.6}, {"text": "is", "start": 78.6, "end": 78.762}, {"text": "cut", "start": 78.762, "end": 79.387}, {"text": "and", "start": 79.387, "end": 79.512}, {"text": "they", "start": 79.512, "end": 79.65}, {"text": "can't", "start": 79.65, "end": 79.95}, {"text": "talk", "start": 79.95, "end": 80.25}, {"text": "to", "start": 80.25, "end": 80.337}, {"text": "each", "start": 80.337, "end": 80.512}, {"text": "other", "start": 80.512, "end": 81.25}]}, {"index": 9, "kind": "prose", "text": "And here's the thing about that phone line: it will get cut. Cables get chewed, switches die, packets vanish into the void. In the world of networks, the gremlins always strike eventually — usually at 2 a.m., usually right before your launch. A partition is simply two servers that are both alive, both serving customers, but unable to reach each other:", "start": 81.55, "end": 101.85, "words": [{"text": "And", "start": 81.8, "end": 81.925}, {"text": "here's", "start": 81.925, "end": 82.188}, {"text": "the", "start": 82.188, "end": 82.275}, {"text": "thing", "start": 82.275, "end": 82.462}, {"text": "about", "start": 82.462, "end": 82.75}, {"text": "that", "start": 82.75, "end": 82.975}, {"text": "phone", "start": 82.975, "end": 83.225}, {"text": "line", "start": 83.225, "end": 83.775}, {"text": "it", "start": 83.775, "end": 83.938}, {"text": "will", "start": 83.938, "end": 84.05}, {"text": "get", "start": 84.05, "end": 84.25}, {"text": "cut", "start": 84.25, "end": 85.05}, {"text": "Cables", "start": 85.05, "end": 85.625}, {"text": "get", "start": 85.625, "end": 85.837}, {"